---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { GITHUB_REPOSITORY_URL } from "../lib/site";

const capabilities = [
  {
    title: "One shared task sidebar",
    body: "See the agent threads every teammate starts, who owns them, and what needs attention. Jump into the same run instead of opening another silo.",
  },
  {
    title: "Take a Look",
    body: "Ping a teammate from the agent answer that needs judgment. They land on the exact thread and can continue the conversation with the agent.",
  },
  {
    title: "Talk beside the run",
    body: "Keep questions, links, and corrections in a durable team discussion attached to the agent thread that produced them.",
  },
  {
    title: "Private briefing",
    body: "Ask a temporary, read-only assistant to catch you up. Its answers stay private to you and never pollute the shared conversation.",
  },
  {
    title: "PR review threads",
    body: "Use Review beside a pull request link to start a dedicated review thread, with a distinct icon and status in the sidebar.",
  },
  {
    title: "Presence and shared control",
    body: "See who is already there, then send, interrupt, redirect, resume, or archive the same long-running agent work together.",
  },
] as const;

const quickstart = `git clone https://github.com/astraly-labs/campfire.git
cd campfire
corepack enable
corepack pnpm install --frozen-lockfile
corepack pnpm dev`;
---

<Layout>
  <section class="hero section-shell">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">Open source · T3 Code, now multiplayer</p>
      <h1>The agent workspace was already here. We brought the team into it.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Campfire is a thin fork of T3 Code for small, fully trusted teams: shared agent threads,
        presence, Take a Look, side discussions, review chats, and private briefings — without
        turning agent work into another Slack.
      </p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button primary" href={GITHUB_REPOSITORY_URL}>View on GitHub</a>
        <a class="button secondary" href="#quickstart">Read the quickstart</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <aside class="near-fold-credit" aria-labelledby="near-fold-credit-title">
      <p class="eyebrow" id="near-fold-credit-title">Built on T3 Code</p>
      <p>
        The provider integrations, remote architecture, worktrees, and core clients are upstream
        work by <a href="https://github.com/juliusmarminge">Julius Marminge</a>,
        {" "}<a href="https://github.com/t3dotgg">Theo Browne</a>, the pingdotgg maintainers, and
        contributors.
      </p>
      <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/pingdotgg/t3code">Visit T3 Code ↗</a>
      <small>Campfire is independently maintained and is not endorsed by T3 Tools Inc.</small>
    </aside>
  </section>

  <figure class="product-proof page-shell">
    <div class="screenshot-frame">
      <video
        aria-label="Campfire demo showing shared agent threads, a Take a Look handoff, direct teammate control, and team discussion"
        autoplay
        controls
        muted
        playsinline
        width="1600"
        height="1000"
      >
        <source src="/campfire-feature-reveal.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
      </video>
    </div>
    <figcaption>
      Every teammate's runs in one sidebar, Take a Look, direct agent control, and a side discussion:
      the T3 Code workspace becomes a shared room.
    </figcaption>
  </figure>

  <section class="thesis section-shell">
    <header class="section-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">Agent-first collaboration</p>
      <h2>Don’t rebuild Slack around agents. Make the agent workspace multiplayer.</h2>
      <p>
        Chat-first tools pull agent work back into another channel. Campfire takes the opposite bet:
        start with T3 Code’s purpose-built agent workspace, then bring your teammates into it. The
        run, its controls, and the human decisions around it stay together.
      </p>
    </header>
  </section>

  <section id="product" class="capabilities section-shell">
    <header class="section-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">The team layer</p>
      <h2>The workflows we wanted from an agent workspace.</h2>
    </header>

    <dl>
      {capabilities.map((capability) => (
        <div>
          <dt>{capability.title}</dt>
          <dd>{capability.body}</dd>
        </div>
      ))}
    </dl>

    <div class="fork-note">
      <p class="eyebrow">A fork, on purpose</p>
      <p>
        Staying close to upstream does not mean staying frozen. T3 Code can remain focused while
        Campfire ships opinionated workflows for teams who live in it all day. The code is open:
        add the feature your team needs, keep it local, or upstream the parts that generalize.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p class="upstream-note">
      Codex, Claude Code, Cursor, Grok Build, and OpenCode support, along with remote sessions,
      worktrees, and the web, desktop, and early mobile clients, come from T3 Code.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="quickstart" class="quickstart section-shell">
    <div class="section-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">Source first</p>
      <h2>Run Campfire from source.</h2>
      <p>
        Campfire does not have a stable packaged release yet. You need Node.js 24.13.1 or newer
        within major 24 and at least one T3 Code provider already installed and authenticated.
      </p>
      <div class="inline-links">
        <a href="https://github.com/pingdotgg/t3code#installation">Provider setup ↗</a>
        <a href={`${GITHUB_REPOSITORY_URL}/blob/staging/docs/operations/campfire-mac-mini.md`}>
          Trusted-team deployment ↗
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="code-block">
      <div class="code-label">Clone and start the development server</div>
      <pre><code>{quickstart}</code></pre>
      <p>Open the pairing URL printed by the server. Local development state stays in <code>.t3</code>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="trust" class="trust section-shell">
    <div class="boundary">
      <p class="eyebrow">Read this before deploying</p>
      <h2>Campfire has no permissions model. That is the design.</h2>
      <div class="boundary-copy">
        <p>
          There is no RBAC, tenant isolation, or per-user workspace permission. Anyone admitted to
          an instance can see and act on every shared agent thread and every project the Campfire
          service can reach.
        </p>
        <p>
          Campfire authenticates teammates and records who did what. It does not authorize them
          differently. Authentication is not isolation.
        </p>
        <p>
          Run it on a dedicated host behind a network boundary you control, use an explicit identity
          allowlist, and invite only people you would already trust with repository access. If you
          need isolation between users or teams, Campfire is the wrong tool.
        </p>
        <a class="text-link" href={`${GITHUB_REPOSITORY_URL}/blob/staging/SECURITY.md`}>
          Read the security model →
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="upstream" class="upstream section-shell">
    <header class="section-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">Upstream</p>
      <h2>T3 Code did the hard part.</h2>
    </header>
    <div class="upstream-copy">
      <p>
        Campfire exists because <a href="https://github.com/pingdotgg/t3code">T3 Code</a> built an
        excellent open-source foundation for driving Codex, Claude Code, Cursor, Grok Build, and
        OpenCode from web, desktop, and mobile clients. The architecture, provider integrations,
        remote workflow, worktree handling, and substantial portions of this repository are the work
        of <a href="https://github.com/juliusmarminge">Julius Marminge</a>,
        {" "}<a href="https://github.com/t3dotgg">Theo Browne</a>, the T3 Code maintainers, and
        {" "}<a href="https://github.com/pingdotgg/t3code/graphs/contributors">upstream contributors</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our strategy is minimal divergence. We rebase onto upstream regularly, avoid renames and
        rewrites that create conflicts for no user-visible gain, contribute broadly useful fixes
        upstream when practical, and keep Campfire-only behavior at narrow boundaries.
      </p>
      <p class="independent">
        Campfire is independently maintained and is not affiliated with, sponsored by, or endorsed
        by T3 Tools Inc. T3 Code and related names and marks belong to their respective owners.
      </p>
      <div class="inline-links">
        <a href="https://github.com/pingdotgg/t3code">Star T3 Code ↗</a>
        <a href={`${GITHUB_REPOSITORY_URL}/blob/staging/NOTICE.md`}>Read NOTICE.md →</a>
        <a href={`${GITHUB_REPOSITORY_URL}/blob/staging/docs/UPSTREAM.md`}>
          Read our upstream policy →
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .page-shell {
    width: min(1180px, calc(100% - 24px));
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .section-shell {
    width: min(860px, calc(100% - 48px));
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .section-shell {
    padding: 96px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .hero {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 260px;
    gap: clamp(48px, 8vw, 72px);
    align-items: end;
    padding-top: 120px;
    padding-bottom: 96px;
    border-top: 0;
  }

  .hero-copy {
    max-width: 720px;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    color: var(--ember-soft);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    line-height: 1.4;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  h1,
  h2 {
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  h1 {
    max-width: 620px;
    margin-top: 24px;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 4.4vw, 3.4rem);
    font-weight: 450;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    line-height: 1.05;
  }

  h2 {
    margin-top: 14px;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 3.4vw, 2.8rem);
    font-weight: 450;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    line-height: 1.08;
  }

  .lede {
    max-width: 650px;
    margin-top: 28px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 1.7vw, 1.2rem);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .actions,
  .inline-links {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 12px 22px;
  }

  .actions {
    margin-top: 32px;
  }

  .button {
    display: inline-block;
    padding-bottom: 2px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid currentColor;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .button:hover {
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .button.primary {
    color: var(--ember);
  }

  .near-fold-credit {
    padding-top: 22px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
  }

  .near-fold-credit > p:not(.eyebrow) {
    margin-top: 18px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .near-fold-credit p a,
  .upstream-copy p a {
    color: var(--text);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-color: var(--line-strong);
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .near-fold-credit small {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 18px;
    color: var(--dim);
    font-size: 12px;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .text-link,
  .inline-links a {
    color: var(--ember-soft);
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .text-link {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: 20px;
  }

  .text-link:hover,
  .inline-links a:hover,
  .near-fold-credit p a:hover,
  .upstream-copy p a:hover {
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .product-proof {
    padding-bottom: clamp(72px, 9vw, 112px);
  }

  .screenshot-frame {
    overflow: hidden;
    padding: clamp(8px, 1.6vw, 18px);
    background: #edf1fa;
  }

  .screenshot-frame :global(video) {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
    background: #fff;
  }

  figcaption {
    max-width: 680px;
    margin-top: 18px;
    color: var(--dim);
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .section-intro {
    max-width: 720px;
  }

  .section-intro > p:not(.eyebrow) {
    max-width: 640px;
    margin-top: 22px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .capabilities dl {
    margin-top: 56px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .capabilities dl > div {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(200px, 0.65fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 24px 48px;
    padding: 24px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .capabilities dt {
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 650;
  }

  .capabilities dd,
  .upstream-note {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .upstream-note {
    max-width: 740px;
    margin-top: 30px;
  }

  .fork-note {
    max-width: 740px;
    margin-top: 42px;
    padding: 26px 28px;
    background: var(--surface);
  }

  .fork-note > p:last-child {
    margin-top: 12px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .quickstart,
  .upstream {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.85fr) minmax(420px, 1.15fr);
    gap: clamp(48px, 8vw, 108px);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .quickstart .inline-links {
    margin-top: 24px;
  }

  .code-block {
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
    background: var(--surface);
  }

  .code-label {
    padding: 12px 16px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    color: var(--dim);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.07em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  pre {
    overflow-x: auto;
    padding: 22px 20px;
    color: var(--text);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    tab-size: 2;
  }

  .code-block > p {
    padding: 14px 16px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    color: var(--dim);
    font-size: 12px;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .code-block p code {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
  }

  .boundary {
    padding-left: clamp(22px, 4vw, 44px);
    border-left: 1px solid var(--ember);
  }

  .boundary h2 {
    max-width: 760px;
  }

  .boundary-copy {
    max-width: 750px;
    margin-top: 34px;
  }

  .boundary-copy p,
  .upstream-copy p {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .boundary-copy p + p,
  .upstream-copy p + p {
    margin-top: 18px;
  }

  .upstream-copy {
    padding-top: 26px;
  }

  .upstream-copy .independent {
    color: var(--dim);
    font-size: 13px;
  }

  .upstream-copy .inline-links {
    margin-top: 28px;
  }

  @keyframes scroll-reveal {
    from {
      opacity: 0;
      transform: translateY(18px);
    }

    to {
      opacity: 1;
      transform: translateY(0);
    }
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
    @supports (animation-timeline: view()) {
      .product-proof,
      .section-intro,
      .capabilities dl > div,
      .fork-note,
      .code-block,
      .boundary,
      .upstream-copy {
        animation: scroll-reveal linear both;
        animation-timeline: view();
        animation-range: entry 8% cover 30%;
      }
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .hero,
    .quickstart,
    .upstream {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .hero {
      align-items: start;
    }

    .near-fold-credit {
      max-width: 640px;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 620px) {
    .page-shell {
      width: calc(100% - 16px);
    }

    .section-shell {
      width: min(100% - 32px, 860px);
    }

    h1 {
      font-size: clamp(2.15rem, 11vw, 3.1rem);
    }

    .actions {
      align-items: stretch;
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .capabilities dl > div {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 8px;
    }

    .boundary {
      padding-left: 20px;
    }
  }
</style>
